Media type name: application

Media subtype name: vnd.krypteon.krpt

Required parameters: N/A

Optional parameters: N/A

Encoding considerations: binary

Security considerations:

Media does not contain active or executable content.

Media provides privacy and integrity through its own cryptographic mechanisms.

Media data is encrypted and plain-text header does not contain any reference to user/creator identity. All parts have separate CRC checksum.

Media uses a completely new proprietary format.

Media does not incorporates links.

Normally, only a very small part of the header isn't encrypted. Filename(s), dates, filetype(s), CRCs, etc, are encrypted with a diffent key than the file data. Integrity and tampering are protected and garanteed by multi-layer CRCs, which are all encrypted making them impossible to read or write by hackers. That (normally, see below) doesn't protect the integrity from media support unrecoverable errors or failure.

In case of data corruption, only the corrupted bits are unrecoverable; the rest of the file can still be decrypted and opened. For very important data, users are stronlgy advised to chose our optional Reed-Solomon 4+2 ECC encoding at the cost of 50% data space overhead (which may be slightly compensated by our optional compression). Our in-app help and video tutorial also suggest strategies like redundant data storage and backup for important data storage.

Normally, there is no input of password or seed selection of any kind needed; but if high or extreme mode is selected, a PIN, password or passphrase, and/or a seed selection may have to be input for both encryption and decryption. In high/extreme mode, users risk losing there data eternally if they lose the security input.

Interoperability considerations: The format is intended to be normally processed by Krypteon™ and other compatible Yagro électronique Inc software and hardware products. No known interoperability issues with standard file transfer protocols (HTTP, WebSocket, FTP, email attachments, etc.) have been identified. Older versions of the format (using other file extension) are not supported.

Published specification: No publication of specifications is planned at this time. We may publish (or not) if we eventually offer SKD to third parties. Full security audit and report shall be performed by Anthropic's Claude Mythos under strict NDA without revealing specs to the public. Part of specifications shall eventually be published within patent appilcation.

Applications which use this media: Krypteon encryption / secure teamwork / communication software, and other compatible Yagro électronique Inc software and hardware

Fragment identifier considerations: None

Restrictions on usage: Usage should be limited, as much as possible, to Krypteon encryption / secure teamwork / communication software / data management, other compatible Yagro électronique Inc software and hardware with valid license, and probably, in the future, by third party applications under SDK agreement.

